2026-06-04 11:39:42,040 | AGENT | Final proposal generated: # 1. Executive Summary
The City of Belval is seeking a comprehensive artificial intelligence (AI) solution to assist its municipal agents in their daily tasks, enhancing efficiency, information access, and service quality. Our consortium, comprised of specialized agents, proposes a tailored AI-powered assistance tool that integrates with existing systems, adheres to stringent GDPR requirements, and prioritizes sovereignty, security, innovation, and sustainability.

# 2. Understanding of Requirements
The City of Belval's call for tenders outlines specific objectives: to design, implement, and deploy an AI solution assisting municipal agents in accessing information, drafting documents, processing files, and suggesting actions, all while ensuring GDPR compliance, high availability, performance, integration with existing systems, sovereignty over data, budgetary efficiency, and environmental sustainability.

# 3. Proposed Solution
Our proposed solution leverages a sovereign large language model, Mistral 7B Instruct, which is self-hostable and compliant with EU regulations due to its Apache 2.0 license. This model will be fine-tuned using methods like LoRA or QLoRA on domain-specific corpora to adapt the tone and format of generated texts to the users' needs. For information retrieval, we will utilize Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities, including dense vector semantic retrieval and hybrid strategies, ensuring accurate and relevant results from large knowledge bases.

To meet the requirement for explicability and transparency, our solution includes explainability methods that allow for understanding the elements leading to an answer or suggestion. The system will be designed as a tool of assistance, with no automated decisions without explicit validation by an agent, adhering to Article 6(1)(e) of the GDPR.

For hosting, we will partner with green hosting providers like OVHcloud or Scaleway, utilizing 100% renewable energy and reducing carbon impact. Digital sobriety practices will include INT8/INT4 model quantisation for a 40% reduction in GPU energy consumption, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching for an estimated 20% reduction in recomputes, and a green IT hardware procurement policy ensuring a minimum 5-year lifecycle.

Our technical architecture will integrate with the City's existing information systems using API gateways like Kong or Apigee, message brokers such as Apache Kafka or RabbitMQ, and identity providers like Active Directory or Keycloak. We will ensure high availability through containerization using Docker and Kubernetes, aiming for an availability of 99.9%, and implement monitoring tools like Prometheus and Grafana to ensure our performance metrics are met.

From a legal standpoint, we will enforce contractual obligations mandating human oversight over automated decisions and conduct a Data Protection Impact Assessment (DPIA) if necessary. Our standard data residency policy is set to "EU only," aligning with the client's requirement for hosting data exclusively within the EU.

The budget for this project will be managed to optimize costs while ensuring quality of service, with strategies including renegotiating rates with subcontractors and potentially reducing scope by removing optional modules or training days if necessary. Our pricing model aims for a target gross margin of 28%, with a minimum acceptable margin of 18%.

# 4. Unaddressed Requirements
Given the information provided, all requirements outlined in the call for tenders are addressed within our proposal. However, we acknowledge that specific details regarding the City's current infrastructure and potential integration challenges may require further clarification.

# 5. Conclusion
Our consortium offers a comprehensive AI solution tailored to the City of Belval's needs, emphasizing sovereignty, security, innovation, and sustainability. By leveraging cutting-edge technologies like Mistral 7B Instruct and RAG capabilities, while prioritizing GDPR compliance, digital sobriety, and green hosting practices, we are confident in our ability to deliver a high-quality AI-powered assistance tool that enhances the efficiency and service quality of municipal agents. We look forward to collaborating with the City of Belval to bring this innovative project to fruition.
